<title>GERMANY: Degussa acquires Portugal's Carbogal.</title>
<headline>Degussa acquires Portugal's Carbogal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and metals group Degussa AG said on Thursday it had acquired Carbonos des Portugal S.A. from Portugese state oil firm Petroleos de Portugal S.A. (Petrogal).</p>
<p>Degussa said in a statement that it had acquired all the 97.36 percent of Carbogal that it did not already own. The price was not disclosed.</p>
<p>Carbogal makes industrial carbon blacks with a capacity of 35,000 tonnes a year and has a workforce of 80.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
